# Keep the build context small and avoid shipping host-only artifacts into
# the image. Mirrors the exclusions in .gitignore plus Docker-specific ones.

# --- Version control / local tooling ---
.git/
.claude/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Secrets: never bake these into an image layer ---
# config.py reads GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY/PORT/HOST from the environment at
# runtime (optionally populated from .env via python-dotenv) rather than
# from a file baked into the image, so a real .env never needs to be (and
# must not be) part of the build context. Pass real values at `docker
# run` time with --env-file .env or -e KEY=value instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- Big raw datasets: not needed at runtime, only for one-time preprocess.
# data/processed/ (the small generated artifacts) IS committed and IS
# needed at runtime, so it is intentionally NOT excluded here. ---
*.nc

# --- Non-runtime documentation (keeps the image smaller) ---
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.pptx

# --- Misc ---
*.log
.DS_Store
